Subject count is wrong: this commit adds SEVEN new trap bullets to AGENTS.md (measured from the diff), not nine. The subject came from the branch commit message because gh pr merge --squash on a SINGLE-commit PR uses the commit message, not the PR title - the PR was titled 'Record traps that each cost a wrong conclusion' precisely to avoid the number, and the number still landed. Content is unaffected; main is not rewritten for a subject. Lesson for this repo: on a one-commit PR the commit subject IS the main subject, so the count must be verified before committing, not corrected at PR time.
